    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0204" n="130" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg130"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/5863</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Andrews</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jassy</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-07-06">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received July 17, 4.32 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>90. General Scott<anchor n="2" xml:id="d182-f1"/> accompanied by four officers of
                    his staff arrived on official visit Jassy July 3 leaving same night. Their visit
                    was great success and they were accorded appreciative reception by Roumanian
                    Parliament and their Majesties the King and Queen. General Scott’s speech made
                    to the assembled Roumanian Parliament was greatly appreciated. He reaffirmed the
                    reasons of America’s entry into war and America’s intention of aiding so far as
                    possible the victory of the Allies including Roumania.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Andrews</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d182-f1" n="2" xml:id="d182-f1-content">
                <p>Maj. Gen. Hugh L. Scott, of the special mission to Russia; see <ref
                        target="frus1918Russiav01#pg_109">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1918, Russia, Vol. I, p.
                        109</ref>.</p>
            </note>
